      "Below is a general **prevention and consultation checklist** for recurring **nasal/eye allergy-type symptoms** that seem worse in some indoor environments and during high-pollen seasons.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Important:** Allergy testing can be helpful, but it must be interpreted together with your clinical history. A positive skin test or blood test showing sensitization **does not automatically prove** that a particular exposure is causing your symptoms.\n",
      "\n",
      "## 1) Symptoms to track\n",
      "Track which symptoms happen, how often, and how severe they are:\n",
      "\n",
      "- Sneezing\n",
      "- Runny nose\n",
      "- Nasal congestion or blockage\n",
      "- Itchy nose\n",
